cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it as below. Please also cite the
  underlying PRIDE deposit and any predictor whose output you reuse; the
  citation each one requires is listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
title: >-
  PXD024871 — a preregistered sequence-only CNN benchmark on HLA class-I
  immunopeptidomics
abstract: >-
  A single-cohort, preregistered study of whether a 1D convolutional network can
  distinguish experimentally observed HLA class-I peptides from matched decoys
  from sequence alone, and how it compares with five published presentation
  predictors on identical rows. Primary endpoint AP 0.7551 (99% CI 0.7368–0.7721)
  on held-out biological units. On 165,574 rows common to all systems, four
  independently built predictors span 0.0046 AP while the CNN leads them by
  0.137–0.142 — a pattern the report argues weakens, rather than supports, an
  architectural reading of that lead. Includes the full decision log, the QC
  gates, and the analyses that were withdrawn.
